{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"This session is being continued from a previous conversation that ran out of context. The summary below covers the earlier portion of the conversation.\n\nSummary:\n1. Primary Request and Intent:\n   The user is running a cobbler-scaffold stitch task (#5155) that requires implementing srd009-du requirements R4.1 (exit 0 on success), R4.2 (exit 1 on errors with stderr diagnostics, continue processing), and R5.1 (SIGPIPE handler) in the go-unix-utils project. The task requires modifying `cmd/du/main.go` and `cmd/du/du_test.go`, adding differential test cases, and verifying compilation and tests pass.\n\n2. Key Technical Concepts:\n   - Differential testing pattern: comparing Go binary output against GNU reference binary (`gdu` from Homebrew)\n   - pkg/testutils.RunDiffTests harness with DiffTest structs\n   - pkg/sys.InstallSIGPIPEHandler() for SIGPIPE handling\n   - pkg/sys.Lstat/Stat for file metadata (Blocks, Dev, Ino fields)\n   - pkg/format.HumanSize for human-readable output\n   - Exit code handling: 0 for success, 1 for any traversal error\n   - Hard-link deduplication via Dev+Ino inode keys\n   - LC_ALL=C required for all differential tests\n   - exec.LookPath(\"gdu\") with t.Skip if not found\n   - DiffTest struct: `{ Name string; Args []string; Stdin []byte; Env []string; WorkDir string; ExitCode int; ... }`\n\n3. Files and Code Sections:\n   - `docs/specs/software-requirements/srd009-du.yaml` (read in full)\n     - Contains all requirements R1-R5 for du utility\n     - R4.1: Exit 0 on success\n     - R4.2: Exit 1 on error, print diagnostic to stderr, continue processing\n     - R5.1: Install SIGPIPE handler via sys.InstallSIGPIPEHandler()\n     - Non-goals include --si, --exclude, -D, -L, -l, --time, --inodes, -b, --block-size, -0\n   \n   - `cmd/du/main.go` (read in full, 218 lines)\n     - Already has R4.1, R4.2, R5.1 implemented:\n       - Line 37: `sys.InstallSIGPIPEHandler()` (R5