k is adding/extending differential test cases in du_test.go\n   - Need to determine if du_test.go exists and what tests it already contains\n\n6. All user messages:\n   - Message 1: The full stitch task prompt with extensive project context, SRDs, architecture docs, execution constitution, and task specification for implementing srd009-du R4.1, R4.2, R5.1\n   - Message 2: \"CRITICAL: Respond with TEXT ONLY. Do NOT call any tools.\" - requesting a detailed summary of the conversation\n\n7. Pending Tasks:\n   - Read cmd/du/du_test.go to see what exists (if anything)\n   - Verify/strengthen R4.1, R4.2, R5.1 implementations in main.go (may already be complete)\n   - Add differential test cases for R4.1 (exit 0 on success), R4.2 (exit 1 on error, stderr diagnostic), R5.1 (SIGPIPE handling)\n   - Run `go build ./cmd/du/` to verify compilation (AC1)\n   - Run `go test ./cmd/du/ -count=1` to verify tests pass (AC2)\n   - Run `go vet ./cmd/du/` to verify no issues (AC3)\n\n8. Current Work:\n   I had just read the SRD (srd009-du.yaml) and the existing main.go implementation. I was about to read cmd/du/du_test.go to understand what test infrastructure exists, then implement the required changes. The existing main.go already contains implementations for all three requirements (R4.1 exit 0, R4.2 exit 1 with stderr diagnostics, R5.1 SIGPIPE handler), so the primary work is adding test cases.\n\n9. Optional Next Step:\n   Read `cmd/du/du_test.go` to determine if it exists and what tests are already there, then add differential test cases for:\n   - R4.1: Test that du exits 0 on a valid directory (ExitCode: 0 in DiffTest)\n   - R4.2: Test that du exits 1 on non-existent path and prints stderr diagnostic (ExitCode: 1 in DiffTest)\n   - R5.1: SIGPIPE handling (may be implicitly tested or need a specific test)\n   \n   The task description states: \"Add differential test cases for R4.1, R4.2, and R5.1 behavior\" and files list says `cmd/du/du_test.go` action: modify with note \"Add differential test cases for R4.1, R4.2, R5.1\".\n\nIf you need specific details from before compaction (like exact code snippets, error messages, or content you generated), read the full transcript at: /Users/pdiddy/.claude/projects/-private-var-folders-dl-cbns6zkx7txc7pt64b6cgzp40000gn-T-go-unix-utils-worktrees-5155/f83767ce-002a-4997-8ccd-7d151b8c4400.jsonl\nContinue the conversation from where it left off without asking the user any further questions. Resume directly — do not acknowledge the summary, do not recap what was happening, do not preface with \"I'll continue\" or similar. Pick up the last task as if the break never happened."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"f83767ce-002a-4997-8ccd-7d151b8c4400","uuid":"fd91e6ca-10de-48a6-990e-10a5cd9ce92b","timestamp":"2026-05-14T12:05:12.418Z","isSynthetic":true}
